  "body": "## The report\n\nThe user (v0.26.0) put the origin at the part bottom and made a Wire Contour. The post was blocked:\n\n```\npost blocked - Wire Contour1: work bottom Z-0.000 is below the lower guide Z0.000, outside the guides' reach\n```\n\n## The cause\n\nThe guide-reach law (`check_guide_span` in `crates/app/src/operation/wire_verify.rs`) compared the work with each guide plane with a strict `<` / `>`. The work bottom is the lowest facet Z of the part or stock in world Z. The guide plane is the stated guide Z plus the WCS origin Z. The two values come from two different float paths: the origin is written from a box (the anchor buttons read the stock box or the part bounds, in the setup frame), and the facets are moved by their own transform. They can differ by round-off, for example 1e-12. The strict comparison read that round-off as a gap, and `{:.3}` printed it as \"Z-0.000\". The test reproduces the exact message with an origin at Z1e-12.\n\nThe same strict comparison was in two more places:\n\n- `judge_pose` in `crates/app/src/machine/wire_edm.rs` (a tapered or 4-axis pose against the guides; message \"rides Z-0.000 ...\").\n- the native Agie job check in `crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs`.\n\nThe upper guide had the mirror bug (\"work top Z12.000 is above the upper guide Z12.000\").\n\n## The fix\n\n- `app::machine::wire_edm::GUIDE_REACH_TOL` = `wire_edm::PATH_TOL` (10 nm, the wire path's existing tolerance). No new number.\n- `below_guide` / `above_guide` compare within that tolerance. A NaN height is refused. All three places use them. The span check runs for each wire post (generic ISO, Sodick, G-EDM) through `wire_verdict`; the Agie job check has its own call.\n- `reach_z` / `guide_z` write the message heights. They never write \"-0.000\". When a refused height and its guide read the same in three decimals, six decimals are written, so that a refused gap never reads as no gap.\n- A real gap is still refused by name.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/4039-wire-guide-zero.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the fix: origin Z1e-12, lower guide Z0 gives `work bottom Z-0.000 is below the lower guide Z0.000`. Origin Z-1e-12, upper guide Z12 gives `work top Z12.000 is above the upper guide Z12.000`.\n- After the fix: these cases post. A 0.01 mm gap gives `work bottom Z-0.010 is below the lower guide Z0.000`. A 0.0001 mm gap gives `work bottom Z-0.000100 is below the lower guide Z0.000`. A 0.01 mm gap above the upper guide gives `work top Z12.010 is above the upper guide Z12.000`.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/wire_taper.rs`)\n\n- `a_work_bottom_at_the_lower_guide_is_within_reach`: a vertical and a 3 degree tapered punch post with the origin Z at 0, 1e-12 and 0.1 + 0.2 - 0.3; a 0.01 mm and a 0.0001 mm gap are refused by name (vertical), and a 0.01 mm gap is refused for the tapered cut.\n- `a_work_top_at_the_upper_guide_is_within_reach`: the mirror at the upper guide.\n\nBoth failed on `origin/main` with the user's message, and pass with the fix. The existing guide tests in the same file (`work_below_the_lower_guide_blocks_the_post`, `work_above_the_upper_guide_blocks_the_post`, `guide_limits_use_the_setup_origin_and_include_stock_above_the_part`, `a_uv_offset_past_the_stroke_or_the_guides_is_refused_by_name`) keep their exact messages.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The user's own model and project: the round-off is reproduced through the WCS origin, not through the user's file.\n- The Agie job check has no test of its guide refusal (none existed before). Its change is the same helper call.\n- No real EDM control.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on head `2b38273d6` (log `4039-2b38273d6.log`, first line the head SHA), macOS:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 351 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. It includes `wire_taper`, `wire_verify`, `wire_post`, `wire_4axis` and the other wire suites, and the example catalog suites `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` (all ok).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- P3: no heavy step.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: a part with its origin at the part bottom posts when the lower guide is at Z0; the guide-reach check no longer reads float round-off as a gap, and its messages never print \"-0.000\".\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4039\n",
